  "result": "```json\n{\n    \"smpl.ordering.AppInsightsFilter\": {\n        \"summary\": \"A Spring servlet filter component that integrates Microsoft Application Insights telemetry tracking for HTTP requests. This filter intercepts all HTTP requests and responses to capture and send telemetry data to Application Insights. Key methods include: (1) doFilter() - the main filtering logic that creates RequestTelemetry objects to track request details (HTTP method, URI, query parameters, session ID), measures request duration from start to completion, captures response status codes (success or error), handles and tracks exceptions as ExceptionTelemetry when they occur, and manages the telemetry operation context (setting and clearing operation IDs). The filter only operates when Application Insights is properly configured with a valid instrumentation key. It tracks both successful requests (with actual response codes) and failed requests (marked as 500 with success=false). The init() and destroy() methods are empty implementations of the Filter interface requirements.\",\n        \"file_path\": \"smpl/ordering/AppInsightsFilter.java\"\n    }\n}\n```",
